  "description": "FB-V1 benchmark FL13. Confirmed orders post a ledger entry; when posting fails, the failure is recorded for audit and the confirmation still stands: when an order is updated into Confirmed status, create a PLS FB Ledger Entry whose (universally required) Ledger Code is sourced from the order's OPTIONAL Ledger Code field. An order confirmed with the field blank makes the create fail; the fault connector then writes a LedgerFault audit-log entry instead of aborting the save. The fault is reachable by ordinary input choice, by design.",
